cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these measurements, please cite them and name the measurement style with each figure: agent run or synthetic sweep."
type: dataset
title: "Local AI on AMD: agentic coding with local LLMs on affordable AMD hardware"
authors:
  - family-names: Bennett
    given-names: Kai Felix
repository-code: "https://github.com/KaiFelixBennett/local-ai-amd-benchmark"
url: "https://benchmark.securesight.ai"
abstract: >-
  Local language models measured in unattended agentic coding in VS Code Copilot
  Chat on two AMD machines, a Radeon AI PRO R9700 and an AMD AI MAX 395 (AMD Halo),
  with llama.cpp on the Vulkan backend. Includes the raw llama.cpp server logs
  pinned by SHA-256, the parser that re-derives every agent run speed figure from
  them, the source code of every game the models built, the launch configurations
  and the agent harness.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - Vulkan
  - AMD
  - Strix Halo
  - Radeon AI PRO R9700
  - local LLM
  - agentic coding
  - benchmark
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
